# Unified diff of our NPWD patch vs shipped upstream 3.15.1-beta.2.
#
# File: dist/html/assets/__federation_shared_react-router-dom-lifestate-backfix.js
# (federation chunk carrying react-router-dom 5.x and its history package,
# minified single line). Verified against the installed bundle before applying.
#
# !!! SUPERSEDES the first goBack-fallback patch !!!
#
# The FIRST version of this patch added
#     var npwdIxA=A.indexOf(F.location.key)
# to goBack and kept the chunk's original hashed filename. BOTH parts failed
# live:
#   1. Same filename + FiveM/CEF asset cache => the phone kept running the
#      UNPATCHED chunk even after `restart npwd`. Never patch a chunk in place;
#      rename it and update every reference.
#   2. The keys-array depth assumption (`A.indexOf(F.location.key)`) did not
#      hold for the live navigation flow, so even the loaded patch could not
#      fix the back arrow.
#
# v2 (this patch) = route-aware behavior + cache-busted filename.
#
# PURPOSE — global phone Back-button fix (bottom-right chevron, Backspace key,
# and every per-app header back button; they all converge on the hash history's
# goBack `k()`):
#
#   PATH "/"                     -> no-op (already home; no loop)
#   APP ROOT (1 segment, e.g. /npwd_lifestate_ojol_customer, /settings)
#                                -> push("/") i.e. the router's own `w(d,h)`
#   NESTED PATH (2+ segments, e.g. /npwd_lifestate_app_store/details/ojol)
#                                -> normal go(-1); 120 ms later, if the route
#                                   is still IDENTICAL (no usable history
#                                   entry, e.g. a direct-open nested route),
#                                   fall back to push("/").
#
# No browser history.length, no keys-array indexing. `F` is the closure's
# current-location ref, `R(d)` is `go`, `w(d,h)` is `push` (verified in the
# installed minified bundle: push writes A.slice/A.push, replace rewrites A[W]).

@@ fragment 1: hash-history goBack gains route-aware fallback @@
-function R(d){t.go(d)}function k(){R(-1)}
+function R(d){t.go(d)}function k(){var npwdP=F.location.pathname;if(npwdP==="/")return;var npwdSeg=npwdP.split("/").filter(Boolean).length;if(npwdSeg<=1){w("/");return}var npwdBefore=F.location.pathname;R(-1);setTimeout(function(){var npwdNow=F.location.pathname;npwdNow===npwdBefore&&w("/")},120)}

@@ fragment 2: cache-busting rename (this is what makes the fix actually load) @@
-  file: __federation_shared_react-router-dom-770100b8.js
+  file: __federation_shared_react-router-dom-lifestate-backfix.js
   and the single reference to that filename in EACH of:
     dist/html/assets/index-ebf41f23.js
     dist/html/assets/__federation_fn_import.js

# Notes:
# - `npwdP`/`npwdSeg`/`npwdBefore`/`npwdNow` are deliberately ugly to stay
#   collision-free in the minified scope.
# - The 120 ms check is a one-shot setTimeout, not a polling loop; if go(-1)
#   navigated, F.location changed and the fallback never fires.
# - Only the hash history is patched; the memory history goBack (function
#   L(){P(-1)}) stays as shipped because nothing renders <MemoryRouter>.
# - The grid button (n=()=>{a||e.push("/")}) and center close button
#   (closePhone) are untouched.

## Re-applying after an NPWD update
#
# 1. In the new federation chunk (name will change), locate the hash history:
#    grep -oE 'goBack:[A-Za-z0-9_$]+,goForward' <chunk>.js
#    then that identifier's definition: function <id>(){<goId>(-1)}
# 2. Identify the closure's current-location ref (the variable read as
#    <ref>.location.pathname in push/replace), the go function (R-style) and
#    the push function (w-style, the one that slices+pushes the keys array).
# 3. Apply fragment 1 with those real identifiers. Depth = number of non-empty
#    path segments; <= 1 and not "/" -> push("/"); nested -> go(-1) + 120 ms
#    unchanged-route fallback to push("/").
# 4. RENAME the chunk (fragment 2) and update EVERY reference to the old
#    filename across dist/html. Do NOT keep the original filename: CEF will
#    serve the stale cached asset and the patch will silently not run.
# 5. Restart npwd. Verify the back arrow works BEFORE blaming the algorithm —
#    if it still does nothing, the old filename is being served.
